# Agent shims: the one list of commands Tether wraps for agent panes.
#
# Each line is: <command> <action> <argument...>. The installer links
# ~/.local/lib/tether/shims/<command> to tether-shim; Tether puts that
# directory first on PATH in every session it creates. Each shim runs the real
# binary (the next one on PATH) with argv changed as the action says.
#
#   prepend           <flag>                  put <flag> before the arguments
#                                             (systemd-run treats anything after
#                                             its COMMAND as that command's own)
#   after-subcommand  <flag> <sub,sub,...>    put <flag> after the first argument
#                                             when it is one of the listed
#                                             subcommands (udisksctl options are
#                                             per subcommand)
#   refuse            <message>               print the message, exit 126
#
# Why: a system-bus polkit check from an agent process otherwise falls back to
# the owner's desktop session and pops a password dialog. With
# --no-ask-password / --no-user-interaction the call fails at once instead.
# resolvectl has no such flag, so it is not listed.
systemctl      prepend           --no-ask-password
systemd-run    prepend           --no-ask-password
systemd-mount  prepend           --no-ask-password
loginctl       prepend           --no-ask-password
timedatectl    prepend           --no-ask-password
hostnamectl    prepend           --no-ask-password
localectl      prepend           --no-ask-password
machinectl     prepend           --no-ask-password
udisksctl      after-subcommand  --no-user-interaction  mount,unmount,unlock,lock,loop-setup,loop-delete,power-off,smart-simulate
pkexec         refuse            pkexec is blocked for agents; use nightshift request/bypass
